{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"The sun, Earth and moon are round","theme":{"background":"#0b1d3a","foreground":"#ffffff","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c1-p","picto":"globe"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What shape is the Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Round, like a ball","why":"Earth pulls itself into a ball because gravity pulls evenly from all sides.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Flat, like a plate","why":"Pupils see the flat ground and forget how far the Earth curves.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Square, like a box","why":"Pupils mix up the shape of a map or a room with the whole planet.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Spherical"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Shaped like a ball. Every point on its surface is about the same distance from the centre."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c3-p","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What shape is the Sun?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Round, like a ball","why":"The Sun's gravity pulls all its gas into an even ball.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Flat, like a coin","why":"Pupils picture the Sun as a flat disc because it looks flat in the sky.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Long, like a tube","why":"Pupils think of a sunbeam's line and confuse it with the Sun's shape.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c4-p","picto":"moon"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What shape is the Moon?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Round, like a ball","why":"The Moon is pulled into a ball by its own gravity.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Round, like a flat disc","why":"Pupils see the Moon as a flat circle in the night sky.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Pointed, like a cone","why":"Pupils mix up the Moon's crescent phase with its real shape.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Approximately"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-e","content":"Almost, but not perfectly. The Earth bulges a little at the middle, so it is not a perfect ball."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Next Card","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c6-p","picto":"castle"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You find a glowing ball on the castle path. Do you pick it up or call a friend?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Pick it up","why","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Call a friend","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
